    "claim-0": {
      "summary": "Two queues of (accept_rate, request) pairs are sorted descending by rate with index tie-breaking, and rows are granted one at a time, so every grant is a prefix over draft positions.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/0"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        4528,
        4774
      ],
      "sha256": "f6b32b11b973e232b0f58ce5d831d407dc0f7c3a69e8ebdbea4bbc16519b5204"
    },
    "claim-1": {
      "summary": "The selection maximizes expected accepted tokens over estimated step time, where step time is a graph-size baseline plus a non-negative fitted slope times graph size plus a sampler term estimated per request count. Because the numerator is an expectation over accepted prefixes, reducing verified rows can reduce accepted tokens while still raising the ratio.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/1"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        4780,
        5203
      ],
      "sha256": "9e1ac5ff7591e91718c61963d5b02a1fa068b78836ce7ab7fb386e18a0fc6bf8"
    },
    "claim-2": {
      "summary": "The search starts with one row per scheduled request and asserts best_bsz >= num_seqs. This is a row-allocation contract, not a measured speed comparison with plain decode.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/2"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        5209,
        5445
      ],
      "sha256": "1f8f92db05af658d3489f9bf005625ad78790ee15c73b5f7d3209be212a26c4e"
    },
    "claim-3": {
      "summary": "The inspected DFlash decode producer samples its configured full width in both paths; variable-length scheduling budgets verification rows. This conclusion comes from sampler.py and DFlash's fixed-width metadata/forward/sample chain, not the non-budgeted verification-length branch.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/3"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        5451,
        5797
      ],
      "sha256": "2b142ab135c6d15843ea4d54d63b8a6baaa7cc52536a005cba155409b72f4312"
    },
    "claim-4": {
      "summary": "The budgeted path is opt-in. DEEPINFER_ENABLE_MTP_VARLEN defaults false while DEEPINFER_USE_NEXTN_DECODE defaults 5, so fixed-width speculation is the default and the budget must be enabled.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/4"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        5803,
        6057
      ],
      "sha256": "924e22e8da54ea15101ec6bb12e39dd6c7414483f3b40a9147e8d7d1df365027"
    },
    "claim-5": {
      "summary": "The source requires later-position confidence not to affect earlier verification decisions. CPU scheduling takes the total budget from N-2 and reads the latest CPU accept_rates for per-request lengths; when a forward is in flight those rates lag. The overlapping ZOS worker redistributes fixed total_q using the previous sampler's GPU confidence before the main forward, then synchronizes corrected metadata before sampling. This source design is not a runtime sampling-correctness proof.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/5"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        6063,
        6615
      ],
      "sha256": "f351acf0f63d60571e42328d75aad0808f83bf2d76aa30421053e50f39fa26d1"
    },
    "claim-6": {
      "summary": "The confidence-head temperature and the request sampling temperature are separate values with separate clamps. The former scales the confidence head's output; the latter is a SamplingParams field. Neither implies the other.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
        "/claims/6"
      ],
      "byte_range": [
        6621,
        6908
      ],
      "sha256": "2ea03595b624ebd9c4ae39da047a8ec3f46eb4ae9dfe986411b3d1079d1e4ad0"
    },
    "claim-7": {
      "summary": "The reject path is gated on draft logprobs being supplied rather than on request temperature, so a request configured as greedy still goes through rejection. This reading is from the gating logic; no run confirmed it end to end.",
      "layer": "L1",
      "pointers": [
